      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Thanks @{5f6be62b15f9fa5364f1834c|full_name}, we took a look and confirmed a confusing behavior on the PlayerTag API. GetPlayerTag appears to return null if called before SetPlayerTag, but if you don't pass a value to SetPlayerTag when you call it through the SDK,it will record an empty string by default. For what I can tell it's been that way for a very long time.\n\nThat said, the persistence update did affect the frame timing of object initialization. Is it possible that something in your script was calling SetPlayerTag without a value before GetPlayerTag was ever called, and something in the persistence update changed that?",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
