  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2024-11-27T03:56:13.052Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Ever since the persistence update, a script of mine has been failing to operate as expected.\n\nUpon further investigation I have found it to be caused by a change to the VRCPlayerAPI.GetPlayerTag default value when SetPlayerTag has not yet been called.\n\nThe default \"unassigned\" value previously was an empty string, since the update it appears that default value has been changed to the null primitive.\n\nI can easily update my script logic to consider the new null primitive default (changing != \"\" to using string.IsNullOrEmpty), but it is a change in API behavior that was not in any change notes that I was able to find.\n\nLess of a bug report I guess, and more of a general PSA + callout to this change that probably slipped under the radar of the changelog documentation effort.",
